{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115898",
      "title": "Directives & Dependency Injection",
      "lectureOrder": 158,
      "videoOrder": 150,
      "sourceHash": "dc60fe26de07a7f5853ea46740297ecd1db9ca633e2ace256779e0993ab47787",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.28,
          "en": "Now last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 6.81,
          "en": "there is one other feature that you can use in Directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.81,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "which you should know about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 11.61,
          "en": "Because you can inject services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.61,
          "end": 15.39,
          "en": "or, in general, things into your directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.39,
          "end": 19.35,
          "en": "just as you can use dependency injection in components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.35,
          "end": 22.173,
          "en": "It's no different in directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.43,
          "end": 26.01,
          "en": "And you could inject any service of your choice here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.01,
          "end": 27.69,
          "en": "like the auth service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.69,
          "end": 32.07,
          "en": "but you can also actually inject the host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.07,
          "end": 34.68,
          "en": "or a reference to that host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.68,
          "end": 38.61,
          "en": "just as you saw it earlier for components as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.61,
          "end": 42.06,
          "en": "in case you want to get access to that host element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.06,
          "end": 44.01,
          "en": "And that's what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.01,
          "end": 46.05,
          "en": "I'll add a new private property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.05,
          "end": 48.72,
          "en": "which I'll name hostElementRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 50.42,
          "en": "The name, of course, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "And I'll then use this inject function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 56.43,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could use the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 57.543,
          "en": "for injecting it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 62.49,
          "en": "and I'll inject an ElementRef here, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.49,
          "end": 65.193,
          "en": "which is imported from Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.35,
          "end": 71.07,
          "en": "Now, that's the same approach we used in a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.07,
          "end": 74.91,
          "en": "to inject the host element of that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.91,
          "end": 77.58,
          "en": "or a reference to that host element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.58,
          "end": 79.173,
          "en": "It's the same approach here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.58,
          "end": 84.81,
          "en": "Now I wanna give Angular, or TypeScript to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.81,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "some extra information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 89.46000000000001,
          "en": "about the type of host element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.46000000000001,
          "end": 91.28999999999999,
          "en": "this directive will be used on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.28999999999999,
          "end": 94.77000000000001,
          "en": "And that's why inject actually is a generic function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.77000000000001,
          "end": 97.14,
          "en": "where you can use these angle brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.14,
          "end": 100.83,
          "en": "to provide some extra type information to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.83,
          "end": 101.78999999999999,
          "en": "In this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.78999999999999,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "I can tell TypeScript which kind of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 109.53,
          "en": "will be available in this host ElementRef property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.53,
          "end": 112.05,
          "en": "after this was injected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.05,
          "end": 115.95,
          "en": "And what will be available here will be an ElementRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.95,
          "end": 118.32,
          "en": "but that in turn, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.32,
          "end": 123.32,
          "en": "is a wrapper object around the host element type object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.56,
          "end": 128.67,
          "en": "And therefore, ElementRef also takes angle brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.67,
          "end": 132.36,
          "en": "so that we can define which kind of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.36,
          "end": 137.04,
          "en": "will be wrapped by this ElementRef wrapper object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.04,
          "end": 141.18,
          "en": "And here that will be an HTML AnchorElement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.18,
          "end": 142.8,
          "en": "because we know that this directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.8,
          "end": 144.6,
          "en": "is used on an anchor element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.6,
          "end": 146.7,
          "en": "so when we inject the host element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.7,
          "end": 151.113,
          "en": "that will be an HTML AnchorElement type of value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.15,
          "end": 153.99,
          "en": "Well, and with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.99,
          "end": 156.39,
          "en": "we could use this host ElementRef here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.39,
          "end": 158.13,
          "en": "instead of event target",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.13,
          "end": 162.183,
          "en": "in our unconfirmed leave page method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 167.043,
          "en": "So there we could use this.hostElementRef nativeElementRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.79,
          "end": 174.63,
          "en": "and also use this to update the ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.63,
          "end": 176.223,
          "en": "before we leave the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.29,
          "end": 182.013,
          "en": "So we can use this injected host element reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.3,
          "end": 186.3,
          "en": "And with that, if we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.3,
          "end": 189.39,
          "en": "if I click here and I confirm this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.39,
          "end": 192.6,
          "en": "this still works the way it did before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.6,
          "end": 196.05,
          "en": "this query parameter is still being added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.05,
          "end": 199.143,
          "en": "but now with help of the injected host element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.12,
          "end": 204.57,
          "en": "And that, therefore, hopefully gives you a good idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.57,
          "end": 207.96,
          "en": "of what you can do with attribute directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.96,
          "end": 209.88,
          "en": "and when you might want to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.88,
          "end": 211.92000000000002,
          "en": "a custom attribute directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.92000000000002,
          "end": 214.62,
          "en": "Though, I'll also say it right away,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.62,
          "end": 217.8,
          "en": "that in most Angular applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.8,
          "end": 222.8,
          "en": "you will probably only build a few attribute directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.87,
          "end": 226.29,
          "en": "and you'll mostly work with components instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.29,
          "end": 229.8,
          "en": "Directives are a key Angular feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 233.94,
          "en": "but they're not a feature you're going to use all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.94,
          "end": 238.07999999999998,
          "en": "Instead, the main feature really are components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.07999999999998,
          "end": 239.61,
          "en": "Nonetheless, directives matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 239.61,
          "end": 243.81,
          "en": "and this here was just one type of directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.81,
          "end": 247.653,
          "en": "Next, let's build a custom structural directive.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
